    "text": [
      "You cannot rob us of the rights we cherish,",
      "Nor turn our thoughts away",
      "From the bright picture of a \"Woman's Mission\"",
      "Our hearts portray.",
      "We claim to dwell, in quiet and seclusion,",
      "Beneath the household roof,--",
      "From the great world's harsh strife, and jarring voices,",
      "To stand aloof;--",
      "Not in a dreamy and inane abstraction",
      "To sleep our life away,",
      "But, gathering up the brightness of home sunshine,",
      "To deck our way.",
      "As humble plants by country hedgerows growing,",
      "That treasure up the rain,",
      "And yield in odours, ere the day's declining,",
      "The gift again;",
      "So let us, unobtrusive and unnoticed,",
      "But happy none the less,",
      "Be privileged to fill the air around us",
      "With happiness;",
      "To live, unknown beyond the cherished circle,",
      "Which we can bless and aid;",
      "To die, and not a heart that does not love us",
      "Know where we're laid."
    ],
    "fulltext": "You cannot rob us of the rights we cherish,\nNor turn our thoughts away\nFrom the bright picture of a \"Woman's Mission\"\nOur hearts portray.\nWe claim to dwell, in quiet and seclusion,\nBeneath the household roof,--\nFrom the great world's harsh strife, and jarring voices,\nTo stand aloof;--\nNot in a dreamy and inane abstraction\nTo sleep our life away,\nBut, gathering up the brightness of home sunshine,\nTo deck our way.\nAs humble plants by country hedgerows growing,\nThat treasure up the rain,\nAnd yield in odours, ere the day's declining,\nThe gift again;\nSo let us, unobtrusive and unnoticed,\nBut happy none the less,\nBe privileged to fill the air around us\nWith happiness;\nTo live, unknown beyond the cherished circle,\nWhich we can bless and aid;\nTo die, and not a heart that does not love us\nKnow where we're laid.",
